code: 0
--- stdout
Use it to see what is on the board: one line per open issue, grouped by status
in board order, issues without a status first.

Closed issues and issues in a final status (statuses.final) are hidden and
counted; --all shows them, and so does --status naming a final status.
Issues in a resolved status that is not final (statuses.resolved, such as
Ready: done, waiting for a release) are one line of numbers; --status
naming that status, or --all, lists them with their titles.
Filters combine with AND; the issues they leave out are counted. Only
issues are listed: draft issues and pull requests on the board are counted.

GitHub lists a board's items a few seconds behind writes: an issue just
created or moved may be missing or in its old status. gh dojo show N reads
the issue itself and is up to date at once.

Usage:
  gh dojo list [flags]

Examples:
  gh dojo list
  gh dojo list --status "In progress" --mine
  gh dojo list --status none
  gh dojo list --sprint current
  gh dojo list --label bug --label area:cli --limit 100

Flags:
      --all                  also show closed issues and issues in a final status
  -h, --help                 help for list
      --label stringArray    only issues with this label; repeat to require several
      --limit int            print at most this many issues (default 50)
      --mine                 only issues assigned to you
      --sprint string        only issues in this sprint (fields.sprint): "current" (today, in board.timezone), a title, or "none"
      --status stringArray   only issues in this status ("none": without a status); repeat for several

Global flags: --jq, --json, --template (see gh dojo --help)
